# 2. STRICT DEVELOPMENT RULES

These requirements are mandatory.

1. Use Kotlin exclusively for Android application logic.
2. Use XML layouts for all UI screens.
3. Do not use Jetpack Compose.
4. Use a single MainActivity.
5. Use Fragments and Navigation Component for screen navigation.
6. Implement MVVM with ViewModels.
7. Follow Clean Architecture and SOLID principles.
8. Separate Presentation, Domain, and Data layers.
9. Use Room as the primary local database.
10. Use DataStore for application preferences.
11. Use Hilt for dependency injection.
12. Use Coroutines and Flow for asynchronous operations.
13. Use RecyclerView and reusable adapters where appropriate.
14. Use ViewBinding instead of findViewById.
15. Do not create unnecessary duplicate components.
16. Do not put business logic inside Activities or Fragments.
17. Do not put database queries directly inside UI components.
18. Do not create giant classes containing unrelated responsibilities.
19. Do not hardcode UI values, strings, colors, dimensions, fonts, icons, or configuration values.
20. Every important class, interface, method, and component must have clear English documentation explaining its purpose and responsibility.

